            <div xml:id="d220">

                <pb facs="0213" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/11–2849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-11-28T17:00:00+00:00">November 28,
                            1949—5 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 29—12:30 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4731. According Scarlett, Foreign Office, French Embassy, London, has informed
                    him that Vatican is putting considerable pressure on <pb facs="0214" n="204"
                        xml:id="pg204"/> French Government to recognize Chinese Communists arguing
                    that until France and other nations with influential Catholic population
                    recognize Communists Vatican cannot do so, and until Vatican recognizes
                    Communists it lacks means to oppose communism in China [garbled group]
                    protection Catholic interests there.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 4731, repeated Paris 933.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
